              "instruction": "pañca, then pañcamaḥ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pañca*, then *pañcamaḥ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "which of the two answers how many — pañca",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: which of the two answers *how many* — ***pañca***]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the ending that turned one into the other — -ma",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the ending that turned one into the other — ***-ma***]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is पञ्च plus -म? (पञ्चमः (pañcamaḥ).) Why did this chapter not begin at first? (Because the rule has to be seen before a departure from it can be read as one.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Source: Macdonell, A Practical Sanskrit Dictionary, p. 149 (DSAL)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
