              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "draw the । and say what it marks — R2, five lessons back",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: draw the **।** and say what it marks — **R2**, five lessons back]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say gatvā and name what the -त्वा does — R3, twenty lessons back",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *gatvā* and name what the **-त्वा** does — **R3**, twenty lessons back]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say kiñcit — R4, eighty lessons back",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *kiñcit* — **R4**, eighty lessons back]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: अष्टमः",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अष्टमः (aṣṭamaḥ) — \"eighth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अष्ट + म. Third time, same move."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Eight is where the cousins stop agreeing. Latin's eighth is octāvus — not octimus, not octus, but a shape that matches nothing else in its own row. English says eighth, keeping its own -th."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit does nothing unusual at all here. अष्ट takes -म exactly as सप्त did."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is worth noticing for a reason beyond the word: it tells you that the -म ending is not merely common in Sanskrit but PRODUCTIVE — the ending a speaker reaches for by default, rather than one of several stored shapes. You will meet the one number in this range where that is not true, and it will stand out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A third ordinal for free, and a reason to expect the fourth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "aṣṭa, then aṣṭamaḥ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *aṣṭa*, then *aṣṭamaḥ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "pañcamaḥ saptamaḥ aṣṭamaḥ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *pañcamaḥ saptamaḥ aṣṭamaḥ*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "which language broke step at eight — Latin",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: which language broke step at eight — **Latin**]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is अष्ट plus -म? (अष्टमः (aṣṭamaḥ).) Did Sanskrit do anything special at eight? (No.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Source: Macdonell, A Practical Sanskrit Dictionary, p. 33 (DSAL)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
