              "instruction": "the other नव, the one that means new",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the other **नव**, the one that means *new*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "saptamaḥ aṣṭamaḥ navamaḥ",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *saptamaḥ aṣṭamaḥ navamaḥ*]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 5,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which नव is नवमः (navamaḥ) built on? (The one that means nine.) What does the other one mean? (New.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Source: Macdonell, A Practical Sanskrit Dictionary, p. 137 (DSAL)."
            }
